  "body": "### Summary\nAs a logged-out reader, when I open a message's or an author's menu, I want to see that blocking needs an account (« Connectez-vous pour bloquer ») instead of finding no Blacklist entry, so that I know how to block someone. Reporting stays available by mail, as today.\n\n### Scope\n- Operator decision D3 of LOT-159 (2026-11-24, #249): with no account logged in, the author/message menus (reader, filtered posts, profile sheet) do not offer « Blacklist » / « Whitelist ». They show a disabled or explanatory entry, « Connectez-vous pour bloquer », that opens the login.\n- The blocklist stays per account (LOT-118). There is no guest list.\n- « Alerter » is unchanged when logged out (mail to the moderators, LOT-159).\n- Legacy shows nothing when logged out: this is a deliberate difference, so it gets a `### Ledger` entry.\n\n### Blocked by\n#1290\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Logged out, every author/message menu shows « Connectez-vous pour bloquer » and no list entry. Logged in, nothing changes.\n- [ ] A view-model test per surface, failing before the change. French string, VoiceOver label.\n- [ ] LOT-159 spec D3 updated to the decision.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
